<h1>Abraham Lincoln’s Colonel John Joseph Coppinger (1834–1909)</h1>
<h2>Colonel John Joseph Coppinger of Cove/Queenstown</h2>
<h3>Early life</h3>
<p>Nothing is currently known of John Joseph Coppinger’s early life, or his education, other than being born ‘<a href="{{ '/families/coppinger/william-joseph-coppinger/' | url }}">Glenmore Cottage</a>’, Cove, 11<sup>th</sup> October 1834, who was one of six children of, William Joseph Coppinger and Margaret O'Brien of ‘Glenmore Cottage’, and cousin of William Coppinger of Barryscourt. This has been fully documented elsewhere within his parents' Coppinger section. Therefore, <strong>cannot have been a native of Midleton</strong> as has been continually misreported in the past until this day.</p>
<p>As may be seen, there is clearly a typing error, but there is no question this is the announcement of the Colonel's birth.</p>
