<h3>Royal Warwickshire Militia</h3>
<p>Likewise, it is unknow when John Joseph took up military service until it was first published, the Lord Lieutenant of the County (William Craven, 2<sup>nd</sup> Earl of Craven (1809-1866)) appointed 'Gentleman' Coppinger, aged 21, to the Royal Warwick Militia, 1<sup>st</sup> Regiment, Ensign, 19<sup>th</sup> October 1855, the lowest rank of commissioned officer. The following year the Lord Lieutenant promoted him to Lieutenant, 2<sup>nd</sup> October 1856.</p>
<p>The 1<sup>st</sup> regiment itself being establised just a few years earlier, 1853.</p>
